diff --git a/docs/spec/radio-features.md b/docs/spec/radio-features.md
index 178d7ca0..c5ab4c10 100644
--- a/docs/spec/radio-features.md
+++ b/docs/spec/radio-features.md
@@ -805,3 +805,7 @@ On the radio (`docs/testing/on-air-coverage.md`, HIL 2026-10-10): zone scan stop
 watch, the battery saver, the 1750 Hz burst and the roger beep on air; TX inhibit and the TOT warning on the radio's
 state; VOX only in silence (the `mic_level` hook is unverified); whether PCM beeps play in FM mode is still open
 (`beep.no_stream` / `beep.blocks` answer that).
+
+### Local M17 data burst for the bench
+
+The optional dedicated M17_PTT_TEST build reserves the radio core's transmitter for one fixed test vector. On an idle simplex FM VFO the monitor contact arms the physical PTT edge. Both contacts must stay down. The provider sends 432 packed bytes at 4800 symbols/s with its native four-level pulse shape. One preamble, one link setup, six data frames and one end marker span twelve 144-symbol modem chunks. The radio core requests power level zero. It closes the session on release, modem completion, underrun, failed queue, transmit inhibit or a 650 ms timeout evaluated by the radio task. Pulse shape and RF deviation require measurement.
